<WikiLayout title="WARDOGS Loadout Builder" description="Plan a WARDOGS loadout by pairing a battlefield role with a budget approach." canonicalPath="/tools/loadout-builder/" pageType="WebApplication" showAd={true} adPlacement="tool">
  <p class="eyebrow">TOOL / LOADOUT</p><h1>Loadout Builder</h1><p>Plan from battlefield purpose first. A useful loadout is a coordinated set of equipment that you can afford to lose and understand how to employ.</p><ToolShell tool="Loadout plan" description="Choose a role and planning profile to identify the guides that should shape your next loadout." leftLabel="Primary role" rightLabel="Secondary focus" options={['Career','Medic','Support','Driver','Pilot']}/><div class="inline-link-row"><a href="/loadouts/">Loadout database</a><a href="/loadouts/budget/">Budget guide</a><a href="/progression/">Progression</a></div>
  <section><h2>Build around a task</h2><p>Choose the role that matches the work you intend to perform near the objective. Medic choices should preserve revive utility; Support choices should account for construction or supply work; Driver and Pilot choices should reflect the vehicle and route. Career is the broad option when you are still learning the match loop.</p><h2>Budget before optimization</h2><p>Persistent cash makes replacement cost part of every build. Start with equipment you can use consistently. Exact item prices that are not documented remain <strong>Currently unconfirmed</strong>, so confirm current values in-game before relying on a precise budget.</p><h2>Review the result</h2><p>Use the selection as a route into the <a href="/loadouts/">Loadouts hub</a>, not as an automatic purchase list. Compare the role guide, expected distance and likely support task before spawning.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>Does the builder calculate a final price?</h3><p>Not when current prices are unconfirmed. It focuses on role compatibility and directs you to version-bound guides.</p><h3>What is the safest beginner approach?</h3><p>Use a modest, familiar primary weapon and only the utility required for one clear job. See <a href="/how-to-play/">How To Play</a>.</p></section>
</WikiLayout>
